  "term": "Montreal Cognitive Assessment",
  "definition": "The Montreal Cognitive Assessment is a standardized screening measure used to identify mild problems with cognition. It looks at multiple areas of thinking, including attention, concentration, executive functioning, memory, language, visuospatial construction, abstract thinking, calculation, and orientation.",
